   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The sky in Spanish",
     "texto": [
      "**What is up there.** The **universo** contains **galaxias**; ours is the Milky Way. The solar system has eight **planetas**. With a capital, **la Tierra** is the planet; with a small letter, **la tierra** is the soil.\n\n**Movement.** The Earth **gira** around the Sun and on itself. The Moon follows its **órbita**. **Estrellas** **brillan**.\n\n**The sun.** It rises and sets. The **amanecer** and the **atardecer** are the two moments of the day.\n\n**The night.** There are constellations, shooting stars and **cometas**. An **eclipse** happens when one body blocks the light of another. Distances are measured in **años luz**. **Gravedad** keeps everything in place.\n\n**Looking.** An astronomer uses a **telescopio**.\n\n**Idioms.** **Estar en la luna** (to be distracted), **pedir la luna** (to ask for the impossible), **nacer con estrella** (to be born lucky)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "«Por... que» and «aunque»: even if it is hard",
     "texto": [
      "To say «no matter how much», use **por** + adjective or **por mucho** + **que** + **subjunctive**:\n\n- **Por brillante que sea**, la estrella no se ve de día.\n- **Por mucho que mires**, no verás el final del universo.\n\nWith **aunque** + subjunctive you speak of something possible but not certain: **Aunque llueva**, saldremos a mirar el cielo. With **aunque** + indicative you speak of something we already know: **Aunque llueve**, saldremos."
     ],
